      "side": 1,
      "message": "Before we get too far here, I prefer we don\u0027t carry on with this change as it is, as `struct pldm_msg` is defined to contain at least 1 payload byte. `payload_length` must therefore always be at least 1, otherwise the caller has created a typed pointer to an object of incorrect size, and that\u0027s a bug in the caller.\n\nNow, `struct pldm_msg` shouldn\u0027t be defined the way that it is, as it\u0027s attempting to describe a flexible array, but the method chosen isn\u0027t the one that\u0027s blessed by the C standard. I need to think about addressing the type problem in the long-term, but in the short-term I\u0027d actually rather the code `assert()` so the callers get fixed, and we don\u0027t add any tests.",
